  "body": "Considering moving out of the city but still wish to be close, Gulf Harbour Marine Village remains one of the best-value boat berthage and living facilities in the greater Auckland area bar none.\r\n\r\n575A and 575B are identical properties featuring three generous double bedrooms, all with their own ensuite bathrooms, a designer kitchen with scullery, double internal-access garaging, ducted air conditioning, and premium chattels and finishes throughout.\r\n\r\nEasterly facing, each home enjoys tranquil views across the western arm of the waterway - perfect for those who want to live in Auckland, without feeling like they are in Auckland.(who wants to be there when you have this for a view at a fraction of Auckland's prices)\r\n\r\nA leisurely 10-minute stroll along the Residential Fringe Walkway takes you to local cafe's and bars, reinforcing Gulf Harbour's relaxed, village-style lifestyle. With its coastal European feel, outstanding marina facilities, and still-excellent value, Gulf Harbour continues to stand apart. At just 45 minutes from the CBD(off peak times), and with Penlink well underway, peak-time commuting will soon be around 15 minutes shorter.\r\n\r\nWhen considering the maths, comparable freehold properties in the Auckland CBD or further North would cost well over twice this price if they had the same facilities\r\n\r\nIf boating and escaping Auckland's central traffic congestion are high on your priority list, it's worth asking-why consider Omaha, Mangawhai Heads, or One Tree Point? Each involves longer drive times and significantly higher price points, without the convenience of true lock-and-leave marina living.  \r\nBerths, there are three options.  Purchase a 12m for $100,000 or 14m berth for just under $200,000 or alternatively if you do not require a berth then we can accommodate that also, it's your choice.  Compared to Auckland marina pricing, Gulf Harbour annual berth cost is a far cry from Auckland's.\r\n\r\nOpen Home Sunday 15th of November from 1.00 - 1.45\r\nCall Roger Sumich on 029 666 66 66 -  Emma Miller on 021 392-262 or Alex Liu on 0274 4666661 for more details",
